From 2efa6f8dc1ee47d6786700bf77e9dafb7d47f116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Matuszewski <xanewok@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:30:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cuda : keep the multi-query q8_0 MMA FA path free of
 single-query decode code

The grouped one-row q8_0 flash attention added byte strides, per-iteration chunk
guards, a sink mask and a partial-tile fallback to the shared flash_attn_ext_f16
template. That template also builds the multi-query verify instances
<256,256,4|8,8,Q8_0>, which gained about 5% instructions, more local memory
traffic and more branches although they never run the one-row code.

Select the one-row code with a compile-time predicate on the instance
(flash_attn_ext_f16_q8_0_one_row) so the verify instances compile the previous
whole-row staging code with half2 strides, the nstages kernel guard and no sink mask.

Fixup for "cuda : add grouped one-row q8_0 flash attention".
